  "kind": "quirk",
  "title": "Excel 16.0.20527 rejects DATE with year >= 10000 even when negative month/day offsets roll back below 10000, differing from build 20430",
  "statement": "Across 22 witness rows in crates/calc-func/witness-differences.tsv, Excel 16.0.20430 rolled negative month or day offsets back from year 10000 (or 9999.9999999) into 9999 and returned a valid serial (for example DATE(10000, 0, 0) = 2958434, 9999-11-30), whereas Excel 16.0.20527 rejects year >= 10000 before month/day normalization and returns #NUM! on all 22 rows.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured across all 22 DATE differences in crates/calc-func/witness-differences.tsv comparing Excel 16.0.20430 against Excel 16.0.20527 (dc-iuwct.36; full bank 22,250 of 22,250 matched on 20527).",
